															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1267048&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606164157" alt="Ihp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1267048)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;" >Ihp</a></span> <span class="odate time_1528511586 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Jun 2018 02:33</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3829628">
									

<p>This is born of my childhood fascination with Shonen battle game anime&#8212; specifically, the trope you see in a lot of them where not only are the magical beasts in the cards/tops/marbles real, but they're capable of having measurable effects on the environment despite being holographic/otherwise immaterial. Seriously, Duel Monsters is a dangerous game even if you're <em>not</em> battling on the back of a blimp with an Egyptian pharaoh.</p>
<p>Anyway, it's half that, half the fact that fidget spinner SCPs haven't really&#8230; worked in the past. I feel like that a lot of the missed the point that they're meant to be toys and little else; so, to skippify them, you want to capitalize on the fact that they're not only toys, but <em>fad</em> toys. Don't tell me that Beyblade wasn't a fad.</p>
<p>Special thanks to DrChandra, stormbreath, Jazstar, A_Sack_Of_Potatoes, and everyone else on chat who critiqued it.</p>

							</div>

								
